{
  "abstract": "Colour the edges of $K_{43}$ with colours $X,Y,Z$, forbidding triangles in $X$ and $Y$ and a $K_5$ in $Z$. Merge $X,Y$ into red and take $Z$ as blue. We classify the merged graphs in which deleting some vertex gives one of the 656 known oriented Ramsey $(5,5,42)$ graphs. Exactly three catalogue graphs admit such an extension. They yield 17 labelled red neighbourhoods for the added vertex and 14 merged graphs up to isomorphism. Their red $K_5$ counts belong to $\\{2,4,10,11,12,13,14\\}$. At every deletion giving a catalogue graph, the deleted vertex has red degree 21, 22 or 23. Consequently, a mixed colouring with a good 42-vertex deletion at a vertex of red degree 24 would certify an unfamiliar Ramsey graph. We give exact models, an exhaustive projection onto the added vertex's neighbourhood, and a reproducible certificate procedure.",
